<title>USA: French Fragrances sells $115 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>French Fragrances sells $115 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from French Fragrances Inc was priced on Tuesday, according to a high-yield syndicate source.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the offering will be used to refinance debt and other corporate purposes, sources said. The company, based in Miami, Florida, manufactures and distributes fragrances.</p>
<p>The deal was increased in size by $15 million.</p>
<p>Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette was lead manager.</p>
<p>BORROWER FRENCH FRAGRANCES INC</p>
<p>AMT $115 MLN	 COUPON 10.375 PCT MATURITY 5/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B2    YIELD 10.375 PCT  PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS    SPREAD 370 BP     CALLABLE NON CALL FIVE</p>
<p>NOTE: Three-year equity call for 35 percent at 109.375.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
